course: dictionary
lesson: 8433
title: Sackful in context
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A sackful is the amount that one sack can hold, or a whole sack full of something. The clue is the word sack inside it. Sack plus full makes sackful, so think of a sack filled to the top.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Each sackful weighs 25 kg» is about weight, so here a sackful is a set amount, like a unit. When you see «a sackful of» with letters or presents, the word means a large amount.
explain: Sometimes the word is used for fun to mean a huge amount. «An Italian nonna loves you a sackful» does not mean she has a sack of love. It means she loves you a lot. Swap in a lot to check: it still makes sense.
fact: A sackful is the amount that one sack holds.
fact: Father Christmas carries a sackful of presents, and farmers carry sackfuls of grain, potatoes or flour.
fact: In maths, a sackful can be a unit, as in «Each sackful weighs 25 kg.»
fact: Informally, a sackful can mean a large amount, such as a sackful of letters.
fact: The plural is sackfuls (or sacksful).
exercise: «Each sackful weighs 25 kg.» What is a sackful in this sentence? | A kind of farm animal | A small bag of sweets | *The amount one sack holds, used as a measure | A cloth made for sewing
exercise: Father Christmas carries a sackful of presents. What does sackful mean here? | *A whole sack full of presents | An empty sack with a hole in it | A list of children's names | A single present wrapped in paper
exercise: An Italian nonna says she loves you «a sackful». What does she mean? | She is carrying a heavy sack | *She loves you a huge amount | Exactly one sack of love | She has lost her love in a sack
test: Farmers carry sackfuls of grain. What does sackfuls mean? | Empty sacks waiting for the rain | One tiny bag of seeds | *Several sacks, each full of grain | A kind of wheat that grows in fields
test: «She has a sackful of questions for her teacher.» What does sackful suggest? | Exactly one question written on paper | A question that is too heavy to lift | A question about sacks and bags | *A large amount of questions
exam: Which sentence uses sackful to mean a large amount? | The farmer filled the sack with flour. | *He had a sackful of excuses for being late. | Father Christmas came down the chimney. | Each sackful weighs 25 kg.
